{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1481440-getting-better-artifacts","id":1481440,"title":"Getting better artifacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-19T03:21:19-07:00","id":1481440,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Getting better artifacts","content":"Just a thought I've had. I have a game going where the PCs have got a bunch of low level artifact weapons and armour and my plan is that eventually everyone that wants artifact weapons/armour will soon get one of each. All good so far and my players, who are new to Exalted, get to play around with the evocation system. However, I'd also like to, eventually, dangle some powerful artifacts in front of my players, level 4 or even 5 monsters. But this will be in the future and I'm unsure how willing my players will be to exchange their artifacts in which they have invested multiple evocations, for potentially more powerful artifacts in which they'll have to reinvest. Essentially they will face losing all the XP they invested in one weapon/armour set for what will initially be a less powerful version (until they buy enough of the more powerful evocations). I'm not sure how willing they will be to do this and how disappointed they'll be to write off a bunch of XP, compared to a character that invested solely in charms.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else faced this and of so what were your solutions, if any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T04:04:20-07:00","id":1481446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1481440-getting-better-artifacts#post1481440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought I've had. I have a game going where the PCs have got a bunch of low level artifact weapons and armour and my plan is that eventually everyone that wants artifact weapons/armour will soon get one of each. All good so far and my players, who are new to Exalted, get to play around with the evocation system. However, I'd also like to, eventually, dangle some powerful artifacts in front of my players, level 4 or even 5 monsters. But this will be in the future and I'm unsure how willing my players will be to exchange their artifacts in which they have invested multiple evocations, for potentially more powerful artifacts in which they'll have to reinvest. Essentially they will face losing all the XP they invested in one weapon/armour set for what will initially be a less powerful version (until they buy enough of the more powerful evocations). I'm not sure how willing they will be to do this and how disappointed they'll be to write off a bunch of XP, compared to a character that invested solely in charms.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else faced this and of so what were your solutions, if any?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn'y worry too much and let the players go with whatever catches their fancy.<br /> <br /> - Some might not care to invest in the &quot;low level&quot; artifacts at all and focus in charms - including some melee charms that may provide the user with essence weapons with evocations of their own - as a safer bet.<br /> <br /> - Some, specially if they are already interested in crafting or sorcerous workings - might tinker with using such artifacts as base components in the making of even greater wonders, making an artifact 4-5 out of one artifact 3 and whatever arcane components/reagents one can get their hands into.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, do remember that it takes Artifact 3 for a wonder to have the capacity for evocations, so low level weapons &amp; armour can be kind of relative.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}